    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "670c138c-920f-33b4-8538-68feaab2e128",
                "word": "peradventure",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "543e9d1d-3f0b-3190-b270-8abd1b184312",
                        "entry_id": "670c138c-920f-33b4-8538-68feaab2e128",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Perchance or maybe; perhaps; supposing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "97ca6125-d448-4d7f-9997-505f1232b6a8",
                                "sense_id": "543e9d1d-3f0b-3190-b270-8abd1b184312",
                                "text": "For be God the Propheit was commandit to stand in the entress of the Lordis house, and to speik to all the cieties of Juda that come to wirschip in the house of the Lord; and was commandit to keip no word aback, gif peradventure, sayeth the Lord, thay will herkin and turne everie man frome his wickit way."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e04e6c0e-576c-49b9-8753-2b449be4d7f7",
                                "sense_id": "543e9d1d-3f0b-3190-b270-8abd1b184312",
                                "text": "Beſides he tells me, that, if peraduenture / He ſpeake againſt me on the aduerse ſide, / I ſhould not thinke it ſtrange, for 'tis a phyſicke / That's bitter, to ſweet end."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4e0c478-5331-4509-b5b1-2eb67bcdd4ee",
                                "sense_id": "543e9d1d-3f0b-3190-b270-8abd1b184312",
                                "text": "Peraduenture there be fifty righteous within the citie; wilt thou also destroy, and not spare the place for the fiftie righteous, that are therein?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5aa25ba-20c3-46ee-bc13-9bdce7e4c8ee",
                                "sense_id": "543e9d1d-3f0b-3190-b270-8abd1b184312",
                                "text": "It may peradventure be thought there was never such a time nor condition of warre as this; and I believe it was never generally so, over all the world; but there are many places, where they live so now."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "58c0f406-f0bb-430f-805b-e51990cf3d54",
                                "sense_id": "543e9d1d-3f0b-3190-b270-8abd1b184312",
                                "text": "Often, too, / The pedlar stopped, and tapped her on the head / With absolute forefinger, brown and ringed, / And asked if peradventure she could read."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "d7146880-9e0c-33f6-b50b-edc03e30a65e",
                "word": "peradventure",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9ac99e8f-4726-4ea6-b2d1-7621f6d1059b",
                        "entry_id": "d7146880-9e0c-33f6-b50b-edc03e30a65e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
